Additional Use Grant: You may make Production use of the Licensed Work if You
                      are an Eligible User and Your use is not a Hosted
                      Offering. Sections 1 to 7 below form part of this grant.
                      Capitalised terms are defined in section 6.

                      1. Eligible Users

                      You are an "Eligible User" if You are:

                      (a) an individual using the Licensed Work for Your own
                          personal purposes, and not for or on behalf of any
                          Organisation (including Your employer or Your own
                          business);

                      (b) an Organisation whose Annual Revenue is less than USD
                          10,000,000 (ten million US dollars) and whose Total
                          Funding is less than USD 10,000,000;

                      (c) a person or Organisation using the Licensed Work
                          solely to document a Public Open Source Project;

                      (d) a school, college or university recognised by the
                          education authorities of its country, using the
                          Licensed Work solely for teaching or academic
                          research, and not for its administrative or commercial
                          operations; or

                      (e) an Organisation in its Evaluation Period.

                      2. Growing past the thresholds

                      An Organisation that is an Eligible User under 1(b)
                      remains one until ninety (90) days after the first of the
                      following to happen:

                      (a) the end of the first financial year in which its
                          Annual Revenue reaches USD 10,000,000; or

                      (b) the date on which its Total Funding reaches USD
                          10,000,000; or

                      (c) the date on which a change in its Affiliates (for
                          example an acquisition) takes it over either
                          threshold.

                      3. Working for clients

                      If You use the Licensed Work for a client's benefit (for
                      example as a consultant, contractor, agency or software
                      vendor), including building, customising, hosting or
                      distributing the Licensed Work or a catalog built with it
                      for that client, Your use for that client is permitted if
                      the client is an Eligible User or holds a Commercial
                      License covering that use. You may rely on a client's
                      written statement of its status unless You know it is
                      wrong. Your own use of the Licensed Work for Your own
                      systems is judged on Your own status.

                      4. Coming into compliance

                      (a) If You stop being an Eligible User (for example
                          because Your Evaluation Period ends), or You become
                          aware (including by notice from the Licensor) that
                          Your Production use is not permitted by this grant,
                          You may continue that use for thirty (30) days (the
                          "Cure Period") in order to obtain a Commercial License
                          or stop that use. Use during the Cure Period is
                          permitted Production use, is not a violation of this
                          License, and Your rights under this License do not
                          terminate during the Cure Period for that reason. One
                          Cure Period applies to each such event; stopping and
                          later resuming substantially the same use does not
                          create a new one.

                      (b) Production use that was not permitted, but that You
                          made before You knew or reasonably ought to have known
                          that it was not permitted, is treated as permitted
                          Production use if You obtain a Commercial License or
                          stop that use within the Cure Period.

                      (c) For a Hosted Offering, the Cure Period is available
                          only once, starts only on notice from the Licensor,
                          and section 4(b) does not apply.

                      5. Guidance and Commercial Licenses

                      The Licensor publishes guidance on this License at
                      https://www.eventcatalog.dev/license-faq (or a successor
                      address it publishes). Where that guidance says a use of a
                      version of the Licensed Work is permitted, You may rely on
