                      A Commercial License or other written permission from the
                      Licensor may permit uses not covered by this grant. A
                      Commercial License held by a vendor or distributor does
                      not cover its customers' Production use unless it
                      expressly says so.

                      6. Definitions

                      "You" means the individual or Organisation exercising
                      rights under this License, and has the same meaning as
                      "you" in the Terms below.

                      "Organisation" means any company, partnership, sole
                      trader, trust, government or public body, or other entity
                      or undertaking, together with all of its Affiliates. A
                      government or public body is treated as an Organisation at
                      the level of the individual body (for example a ministry,
                      department, agency, local authority or health trust), not
                      the wider government of which it forms part.

                      "Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled
                      by, or is under common control with another, where
                      "control" means owning more than fifty percent (50%) of
                      the voting interests or otherwise having the power to
                      direct its management and policies. Two entities are not
                      Affiliates of each other solely because both are owned or
                      controlled by (i) a government or public body, or (ii) an
                      investment fund or other financial investor that does not
                      include them in its own consolidated financial statements.

                      "Annual Revenue" means the total gross revenue (or, for a
                      business such as a bank or insurer that does not report
                      revenue in that form, the nearest equivalent measure of
                      its total income) of the whole Organisation for its most
                      recently completed financial year, taken from consolidated
                      financial statements where they exist and otherwise by
                      adding together the figures for each member. For a
                      government or public body, charity or non-profit
                      organisation, it means the greater of its total income
                      (including grants and donations) and its total annual
                      budget for that year. An Organisation that has not
                      completed a financial year uses its reasonably projected
                      figure for its first year. Amounts in other currencies are
                      converted to US dollars at the average exchange rate for
                      that year from a recognised published source.

                      "Total Funding" means the total amount of equity
                      investment, and of convertible or other investment
                      intended to convert into equity (such as convertible notes
                      or SAFEs), that the whole Organisation has received from
                      investors outside the Organisation since it was formed,
                      measured at the amounts invested. It does not include
                      revenue, government or charitable grants, or loans and
                      other debt.

                      "Production use" means any use of the Licensed Work other
                      than (i) trying it out with sample, test or throwaway
                      content that no one relies on, or (ii) developing, testing
                      or contributing to the Licensed Work itself. It includes
                      running a catalog built with the Licensed Work that an
                      Organisation's employees, contractors or automated systems
                      (including AI agents) use or rely on to document,
                      discover, understand or govern its software systems,
                      whether that catalog is available internally, privately or
                      publicly, and using the Licensed Work in continuous
                      integration or deployment pipelines to build, update or
                      validate such a catalog. Use is Production use if it meets
                      this definition, whatever the catalog, environment or
                      project is called (including "evaluation", "pilot", "proof
                      of concept" or "internal").

                      "Evaluation Period" means the ninety (90) days starting on
                      the date an Organisation first makes Production use of any
                      version of the Licensed Work, or any longer period the
                      Licensor agrees in writing. Each Organisation, including
                      all of its Affiliates, has one Evaluation Period in total
                      across all versions of the Licensed Work. Upgrading,
                      reinstalling, creating another catalog, or a change in the
                      Organisation's Affiliates does not start a new Evaluation
                      Period. If two Organisations that have each started an
                      Evaluation Period become Affiliates, the earlier period
                      applies to the combined Organisation.

                      "Public Open Source Project" means a software project
                      whose source code is publicly available under a license
                      approved by the Open Source Initiative, where the catalog
                      documents only that project's software and not the systems
                      of an Organisation.

                      "Hosted Offering" means using the Licensed Work to give
                      third parties access to the Licensed Work, or to a catalog
                      built with it, as a hosted, managed or multi-tenant
                      service, whether or not for a fee, and whether offered on
                      its own or as part of another product. Members of Your
                      Organisation are not third parties. The following are not
                      Hosted Offerings:

                      (a) publishing a catalog that documents Your own software
                          systems, including making it publicly accessible to
                          Your customers, partners or the public;

                      (b) hosting a catalog for a specific client under section
                          3 as part of services You provide to that client,
                          where the catalog documents that client's software
                          systems and You do not offer hosting of the Licensed
                          Work as a standardised or self-service product; and

                      (c) hosting, without charge, catalogs that document only
                          Public Open Source Projects.

                      "Commercial License" means a written license from the
                      Licensor permitting Production use beyond this grant.

                      7. Everything else

                      All other Production use requires a Commercial License.
                      Nothing in this grant limits the rights granted in the
                      Terms below, including the right to copy, modify,
                      redistribute and make non-production use of the Licensed
                      Work. The content of Your own catalog (the documentation,
                      schemas, diagrams and configuration You create) is Yours
                      and is not part of the Licensed Work.
Change Date:          Four years after the first public release, including any
                      pre-release, of any release in the same release series as
                      the Licensed Work.

                      A "release series" is every release that shares the same
                      major and minor release number, including its pre-releases
                      and patch releases: for example, 5.1 includes
                      5.1.0-beta.1, 5.1.0 and 5.1.3, and they all share one
                      Change Date. Unreleased builds, such as individual commits
                      or nightly builds, belong to the next release series to be
                      released.
